{"term":"ridge","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e7753276782ab8b854","definition":"The back of any animal; especially the upper or projecting part of the back of a quadruped.","example":"He thought it was no time to ſtay, / And let the Night too ſteal away, / But in a trice advanced the Knight, / Upon the Bare Ridge, Bolt upright, / And groping out for Ralpho’s Jade, / He found the Saddle too was ſtraid[…]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Acacia Ridge","Acalanes Ridge","Alpine Ridge","alveolar ridge","apical ectodermal ridge","Bald Ridge","Balmoral Ridge","Barden Ridge","barrier ridge","Basking Ridge","Baxters Ridge","beach ridge","Big Ridge","Blaxlands Ridge","Blue Ridge","bone ridge","Bora Ridge","Botanic Ridge","Bracken Ridge","brow ridge","Bushells Ridge","Butchers Ridge","Carters Ridge","Cato Ridge","Cedar Ridge","combing ridge","Cream Ridge","enridge","Forest Ridge","Gap Ridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ab97540e195af6fbe9","definition":"Any extended protuberance; a projecting line or strip.","example":"The plough threw up ridges of earth between the furrows.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["groove"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Acacia Ridge","Acalanes Ridge","Alpine Ridge","alveolar ridge","apical ectodermal ridge","Bald Ridge","Balmoral Ridge","Barden Ridge","barrier ridge","Basking Ridge","Baxters Ridge","beach ridge","Big Ridge","Blaxlands Ridge","Blue Ridge","bone ridge","Bora Ridge","Botanic Ridge","Bracken Ridge","brow ridge","Bushells Ridge","Butchers Ridge","Carters Ridge","Cato Ridge","Cedar Ridge","combing ridge","Cream Ridge","enridge","Forest Ridge","Gap Ridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org